    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108577" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπο-κλύζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wash from below,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόντος ὑ. χθονὸς ἕδρανα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.663
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τὸ σῶμα</span>
			<i>purge</i> the body <i>by a clyster,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.127c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.</u>
				2.40
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν κοιλίην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					1.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τὴν πόλιν</span>
			<i>flush</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				15.9.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be submerged,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.533
			</span></i> (s. v. l.): metaph., <i>to be flooded</i> with mischief,
				<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nigr.</u>
				16
			</span></i>.</div>
